WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.987
Try it.

2
00:00:00.987 --> 00:00:04.458
Lab 1 runs in PowerShell 7 on
the kit's fictional estate,

3
00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:06.413
with no instance and no tenant.

4
00:00:06.413 --> 00:00:09.508
Go to the kit's folder, and
make this run's results folder,

5
00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:13.774
named for the time you start, so running
the lab again never overwrites a run.

6
00:00:13.774 --> 00:00:16.413
Step one reads the four audited instances.

7
00:00:16.413 --> 00:00:19.375
Only the instances Chapter
1 retained are audited.

8
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:22.754
Look at sequel P R D oh
one: it runs in mixed mode,

9
00:00:22.754 --> 00:00:26.225
zero, while its registry
says Windows only, one.

10
00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:30.300
Sequel F C I oh four is clustered,
and its registry says mixed.

11
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.542
Three of the four engines
run as domain user accounts,

12
00:00:33.542 --> 00:00:35.900
the S V C accounts in the contoso domain.

13
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.921
And sequel P R D oh six,
on SQL Server 2025,

14
00:00:38.921 --> 00:00:44.020
runs as a group managed service account,
whose name ends in a dollar sign.
